{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/450391-can-humans-touch-antlers","id":450391,"title":"Can humans touch antlers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-20T06:56:10-07:00","id":450391,"title":"Can humans touch antlers?","content":"So the Mask is supposed to hide a changeling's true form from sight but what about touch? <br /> <br /> <br /> When a human caresses a changeling's head can he feel the antlers? Or pointy ears or flaming hair or thorny cheeks? <br /> <br /> Do his hands phase through the antlers? Does he subconsciously avoid touching them? If he phases, what would happen if he tried to cut the changeling's head off but missed just above him, would the weapon phase too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5419,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5419-joaov2","user":"joaov2","date":". 03-20-2015, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5419-joaov2","name":"joaov2","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T08:29:16-07:00","id":450475,"title":"","content":"I think this is covered in the description of the Mask in the core book, but the short answer is that the deception is perfectly comprehensive: it doesn't just stop at the visual component. The exact form the Mask takes for concealing something can vary by the entity concealed (and perhaps individual instance of concealment), so long as the end result is, &quot;the mortal finds nothing amiss.&quot; A Changeling with antlers will find a mortal's caressing hand making whatever careful movements are necessary to maneuver around them, or only brushing up against them. The mortal will see, feel, and remember smoothly running a hand through ordinary hair, without any weird contortions or the feel of invisible bony protrusions or whatever. Any mortal on-lookers will perceive the same.<br /> <br /> Phasing isn't really a thing that happens: those parts of a Changeling's body are still solid and real. I think there's an example in there of someone firing a gun at an antlered Changeling. As they're real, solid things, part of one can indeed be broken off by a bullet. The mortal might instead perceive that the bullet had just grazed the target's head, given the Changeling's pained reaction. Any on-lookers will see the same, and I expect remember a consistent injury in the same place. I don't remember what happens with the physical piece of antler, but I think it remains protected by the Mask. If so, whatever means are necessary to keep it undetected will come into play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T10:01:51-07:00","id":450542,"title":"","content":"Oh I see. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5419-joaov2","name":"joaov2","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T10:08:16-07:00","id":450564,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the very example of an antlered changeling is used. :-P<br /> <br /> I think it's explored a little more in Rites of Spring, also. Can't check, right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T11:14:24-07:00","id":450640,"title":"","content":"I wonder though what if a changeling tried to stab a human with her horns could those count has a lethal weapon? And how would the human perceive the attack after being punctured by a headbutt? A spiky helmet? A hidden blade?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5419-joaov2","name":"joaov2","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T12:42:01-07:00","id":450715,"title":"","content":"A Hunterheart could. Getting a lethal damage attack is their thing. Otherwise mostly no unless you take Lethal Mien, then sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T14:05:39-07:00","id":450845,"title":"","content":"If you have a suitable merit or kith blessing, you can do lethal with your antlers. Otherwise, you do bashing. Mind you, antlers are roughly as hard as concrete; I know because to put a hole in a pair of antlers I once helped mount required the use of a masonry bit. You might want to consider whethere or not you really to hit someone with a chunk of concrete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T14:09:10-07:00","id":450849,"title":"","content":"Hrm... I forget, does the Mask extend to contracts and magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T15:20:39-07:00","id":450933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/450391-can-humans-touch-antlers?p=450849#post450849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hrm... I forget, does the Mask extend to contracts and magic?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so... unless it's illusionary stuff that directly uses the Mask. An Elemental who summons fire into her hands looks like a normal person... summoning fire into her hands.<br /> <br /> Maybe there are some exceptions. I think common sense (not the Merit) is the ultimate arbiter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T16:25:05-07:00","id":450973,"title":"","content":"And how would the attack be perceived? Headbutts don't leave puncture wounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5419-joaov2","name":"joaov2","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T18:12:56-07:00","id":451123,"title":"","content":"&quot;Shit, did you see that guy? Head butted that moron clean across the room. Wouldn't expect it from such a wiry guy but I guess he was running on adrenaline.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Funny thing was the amount of blood. Guy's face split open like a water baloon. Big splits in his face. Eye looked like it'd been popped out with a poker. Pressure must've flown IT across the room.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The other guy didn't look too banged up. Thick skull, I guess. Kinda weird shaped head.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, a coroner's report is going to be confusing as hell. They'll assume a concealed weapon must've been involved, regardless of witness statements. But &quot;this is the handiwork of a human being with antlers&quot; is never going to be the logical first assumption. Faerie blunts Occam's Razor to a dull nub.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T18:26:43-07:00","id":451136,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd go with that. Blunt trauma can break the skin, if it's intense enough, after all.<br /> <br /> Sidebar: On first thinking about this, I began with, &quot;Oh, well, maybe there's a little bit of the Mask that applies itself to the injury,&quot; but nah. Because on second thinking about this, it feels like there's far too much danger of overcomplicated and unforeseen ripple effects down that road. I choose to go with the simple and elegant approach that Birnam describes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T00:28:18-07:00","id":452335,"title":"","content":"I know that changeling drones on and on about how the mien is real and the mask is an illusion, I don't believe it means illusionary in the way some people take it.<br /> <br /> Straight from the core book, the mask can be inches shorter or taller or lighter or heavier than the mien.<br /> <br /> If a changeling who is taller in mask than in mien gets stuffed into a space that the mien doesn't fit in but the mask can, if the changeling can't be made to fit, well then you just gave people a full proof way to detect some changelings, not all mind you, but some. Kind of defeats the point of a mask if the mask could be made to detect changelings.<br /> <br /> Another test would be for people who somehow can't reach things they are tall enough to reach because their masks are shorter than their miens. If that works, then the mask fails its job, so much for that perfect protection. <br /> <br /> And well, how illusionary can the mask be if it has a different mass? If it's twenty pounds lighter than the mien, where did those twenty pounds go? If it's twenty pounds heavier than the mien, where do those twenty pounds come from?<br /> <br /> So the mask extends to bathroom scales and pressure sensitive floors.<br /> <br /> It also extends to medical treatment, the book doesn't list so much as a penalty. How can a changeling survive medical treatment if their parts aren't where the doctor thinks they are? <br /> <br /> So the only way that makes sense to me, is that it's more of a quantum thing: A changeling is both mask and mien at the same time, unless they drop the mien, just as a photon is a particle and a wave.<br /> <br /> So if a lover caresses a changeling forehead, they caress a forehead. That doesn't change the fact that the changeling also has antlers, and that the antlers are real, perhaps even capable of doing lethal damage in a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 03-22-2015, 03:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T19:00:50-07:00","id":455223,"title":"","content":"In regards to the medical care and Changelings... it is very rare for a Changeling to have an anatomy so different as to give a penalty to a doctor trying to treat them. Their internal organs may no longer be what they once were (a Manikin may now have a clockwork heart that ticks like a heartbeat), but to a mortal doctor they are still identified as what they should be. A Woodblood may have bark-like skin, but all the surgeon preforming an operation on him would notice is that his skin seems a little tougher or more fibrous than normal... but not enough for him to suddenly say &quot;this guy can't be human!&quot;<br /> <br /> The amount the Mask differs from the Mein is usually a fairly small amount... just enough to make the person appear human. However, some features like huge antlers or horns are not so easy to mask. Most often when something is knocked by such appendages, it will appear that the person is clumsy or some other rationalization will occur. A wind chime that is brushed by antlers is more likely to be attributed to an unusual gust of wind... even from an air conditioner... rather than someone jumping to the conclusion that the person walking under it must have some hidden antlers or horns instead.<br /> <br /> The sad truth is... those Changelings that are so changed by their time in Faerie that they would make it difficult for the Mask to hide their true nature rarely make it back to Earth. They are no longer human enough to make the journey... or haven't remembered enough about what they should be for them to find their way out. Occasionally one might find their way back... but most of these unfortunate souls never return... there just isn't enough of who they were left to make the journey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T22:34:40-07:00","id":455456,"title":"","content":"So, in easy comparison - this in Mien...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/236x/33/89/3c/33893c82a24f0e62c9011913db4d1205.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Humans see in Mask as this...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/images/horncrowngameofthrownsbaratheon_6545.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Or this...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.dailymail.co.uk/i/pix/2011/09/12/article-2036521-0DDAAEA000000578-463_233x396.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> ???<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T23:21:58-07:00","id":455477,"title":"","content":"Or maybe not even that.<br /> <br /> Depends on how much of the Wyrd is flowing through you. At low Wyrd, you look like mostly you, only accounting for the very dire images. In the case of antlers, it won't even register.<br /> <br /> At High Wyrd, well, the latter is more likely, but never deny the possibility of the former.<br /> <br /> You are a water balloon waiting to burst, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T00:35:49-07:00","id":455516,"title":"","content":"Lost on last topic page, bring here to easy conversation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/450391-can-humans-touch-antlers?p=455456#post455456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in easy comparison - this in Mien...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/236x/33/89/3c/33893c82a24f0e62c9011913db4d1205.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Humans see in Mask as this...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/images/horncrowngameofthrownsbaratheon_6545.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Or this...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.dailymail.co.uk/i/pix/2011/09/12/article-2036521-0DDAAEA000000578-463_233x396.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> ???</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T14:55:37-07:00","id":456236,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the whole body sculpting thing could be an easy way to explain the features. Strange, though it may be.<br /> <br /> Of course, you'd have to find some way to convince people why there's a massive convention of body sculptures year round!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T17:07:55-07:00","id":456371,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Mask would make people that conspicuous as a general rule, though I'm also sure some exceptions apply (especially with Striking Looks or a Condition to back it up).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T17:40:43-07:00","id":456390,"title":"","content":"I forgot, do the Lost know what their mask looks like automatically, or do they have to figure that out on their own?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T17:44:38-07:00","id":456391,"title":"","content":"They can strengthen it so it works on changelings and then look in a mirror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T03:30:17-07:00","id":456684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/450391-can-humans-touch-antlers?p=455223#post455223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to the medical care and Changelings... it is very rare for a Changeling to have an anatomy so different as to give a penalty to a doctor trying to treat them. Their internal organs may no longer be what they once were (a Manikin may now have a clockwork heart that ticks like a heartbeat), but to a mortal doctor they are still identified as what they should be. A Woodblood may have bark-like skin, but all the surgeon preforming an operation on him would notice is that his skin seems a little tougher or more fibrous than normal... but not enough for him to suddenly say &quot;this guy can't be human!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Except, again, according to the books, changelings are completely unchanged genetically, with those changelings who do have kids have absolutely human kids, and that vampires can drink changeling blood, the rule isn't &quot;if the changeling would have blood,&quot; changelings are subject to diseases.<br /> <br /> So a vampire can drink woodblood, a fireheart can birth to a completely organic baby after 9 months, a manikin can catch a cold.<br /> <br /> When was the last time you gave your cell phone a cold? How exactly can a baby survive in a humanoid volcano? Do you know many trees that bleed? <br /> <br /> So the mask is fake, except when it comes to blood, reproduction, dna, parasites, bacteria, viruses, genetic conditions..... Uh huh, yeah and maybe someone has a bridge in brooklyn to sell me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T08:43:32-07:00","id":456899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/450391-can-humans-touch-antlers?p=456684#post456684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except, again, according to the books, changelings are completely unchanged genetically, with those changelings who do have kids have absolutely human kids, and that vampires can drink changeling blood, the rule isn't &quot;if the changeling would have blood,&quot; changelings are subject to diseases.<br /> <br /> So a vampire can drink woodblood, a fireheart can birth to a completely organic baby after 9 months, a manikin can catch a cold.<br /> <br /> When was the last time you gave your cell phone a cold? How exactly can a baby survive in a humanoid volcano? Do you know many trees that bleed?<br /> <br /> So the mask is fake, except when it comes to blood, reproduction, dna, parasites, bacteria, viruses, genetic conditions..... Uh huh, yeah and maybe someone has a bridge in brooklyn to sell me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Semi-Relevant Dialogue from an old game:<br /> <br /> Storyteller: So you step out of your ramshackle house into the winter night, shivering under the thorny black sky. Did you have a particular-<br /> Arcane:Wait, wait, wait, why am I cold? My head is <i>literally</i> on fire. I am still burning from the last time I got thrown into the bonfire in Arcadia. I shouldn't be cold.<br /> Storyteller: Congratulations, you have discovered how much your Keeper was a <i>dick</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-25-2015, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T02:00:12-07:00","id":462032,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't even go so far as making the Keeper a dick. The books are clear that during their stay in Arcadia the Changelings were litterally centipeds, birds, flame, but that part of getting back is finding their humanity and changing their bodies to such an extend that they become human again. Those flaming hair don't burn anymore, because the normal world cannot have flames without fuel. In the end, unless your kith, contracts and merrits make it so, the mien is more a scar than a real thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T07:33:27-07:00","id":462227,"title":"","content":"You know that thing where players have conversations for fun mid-game?<br /> <br /> This was that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T15:08:03-07:00","id":462729,"title":"","content":"Whoa, whoa. Whoa. Socializing during a game you are playing with friends for fun? No bueno. What if someone misinterpreted the situation and thought the Keeper was an actual phallus (which is entirely possible). Suddenly the story becomes about the Fireheart, the Keeper's gonorrhea who found its way home. While that certainly opens up the story of seeking out the rubber elemental who probably escaped first, I don't think the player would take kindly to that sort of editing of their character. It's the ST's responsibility to treat all of their tools with dignity and the seriousness it deserves--especially the words out of their mouth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T17:11:25-07:00","id":462847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/450391-can-humans-touch-antlers?p=462729#post462729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the ST's responsibility to treat all of their tools with dignity and the seriousness it deserves...</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait... So he/she needs to treat the Dick Keeper with dignity?<br /> <br /> Now I'm confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T17:30:34-07:00","id":462876,"title":"","content":"The ST should treat their Dick Keeper with the exact level of dignity and seriousness it deserves, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"d